  "body": "This change reorders two steps in the “unload a document” algorithm such that the spec now requires UAs to wait to run any “unloading document visibility change steps” from other applicable specifications (in particular, the Page Visibility spec) until *after* firing the `pagehide` event.\n\nIn practice, in combination with requirements in the Page Visibility spec, this change has the particular effect of stating that UAs must wait to fire the `visibilitychange` event until after the `pagehide` event has fired. That ordering matches the behavior implemented in Gecko and Blink, as well as the WIP implementation in WebKit.\n\nOtherwise, without this change, the combination of requirements with the Page Visibility spec causes the specs together to mandate that the `visibilitychange` event is fired *before* the `pagehide` event has fired (which doesn’t match what implementations actually do).\n\ncc @cdumez\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5949/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 1, 2020, 8:19 AM UTC (7771708)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5949/ff8cb6e...7771708/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 1, 2020, 8:19 AM UTC (7771708)\">diff</a> )",
